1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:27,900
You actually showed up, huh?

3
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:29,820
Didn't you lose badly enough last year?

4
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:32,220
Well, things are different now.

5
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:33,180
Matthew!

6
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,030
I brought you some bug spray and mosquito coils!

7
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:38,460
She's always super nice whenever she sees Matthew.

8
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,380
Captain knows you've been getting

9
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:41,820
all your nutrients getting sucked away.

10
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,700
So he wants to make it up to you.

11
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,110
Is it food?

12
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,580
Monica, if your finger's bothering you,

13
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,400
you can take a break.

14
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:50,460
Thanks, Captain.

15
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:53,340
Hey, aren't you hot wearing that mask all day?

16
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,260
What's it to you?

17
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:56,700
Just make your move.

18
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Episode 14

19
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,380
Wow, that sounds intense.

20
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,700
He's using variations of Twin Dragons Rising.

21
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:12,060
Seems like his specialty is dual-handed play.

22
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:21,180
Captain, what exactly did he say in his letter?

23
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,580
I'll handle it.

24
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,500
Don't worry about it.

25
00:02:26,010 --> 00:02:29,200
One positive, one negative.

26
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:30,760
One light, one dark.

27
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:33,840
One seen, one hidden.

28
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:38,940
The odds of being on the losing end of that are 80%.

29
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:43,260
But if you can play your cards just right,

30
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:49,980
your chances of winning jump all the way up to 100%.

31
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:53,340
It all comes down to timing.

32
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,180
Opportunity knocks but once.

33
00:02:59,080 --> 00:02:59,580
Let's go.

34
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:03,420
Weirdo.

35
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,060
Hey, Sis!

36
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:54,780
What's going on? Why aren't you asleep?

37
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:57,630
Something huge just happened!

38
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:58,140
What is it?

39
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,980
Leo and Mark are both missing at the same time!

40
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,860
What? They're both gone?

41
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:07,740
But don't worry.

42
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:10,140
I already tracked both of them down.

43
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,060
Really?

44
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,420
Sis!

45
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:54,930
There's this super tense vibe,
like something terrible is about to happen.

46
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:55,740
What do you mean "terrible"?

47
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,960
We're facing a formidable enemy!

48
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,580
You always use the wrong words.

49
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,020
What's the difference?

50
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:03,420
Whatever, it's super tense either way!

51
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:36,060
Captain...

52
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:44,630
Hey! The Captain's gone! Look!

53
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,620
What?

54
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,030
He left that early?

55
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,990
He must've gone to find that Masked Guy.

56
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:51,900
We should've gone with him!

57
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:54,300
How could you guys sleep through that?

58
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,220
Why are you yelling?

59
00:05:56,910 --> 00:05:58,620
The Captain was just trying to get your Yo-Yo back for you!

60
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,900
Look, Shawn is missing too!

61
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,660
The one who should've gone didn't make it.

62
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,180
And the one who shouldn't have
gone might make it worse.

63
00:06:11,260 --> 00:06:12,540
Someone with absolutely no skills

64
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,230
tagging along is useless!

65
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:16,380
That Shawn...

66
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,780
He's always causing more trouble than he's worth!

67
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,180
The Masked Guy's letter made it clear.

68
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:23,040
If Mark brought anyone with him,

69
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:25,460
Chuck's Yo-Yo would be gone for good.

70
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:26,390
So what do we do now?

71
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,860
All we can do is wait.

72
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:39,420
He's acting like it's no big deal.

73
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,900
First the Coach is gone,

74
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:15,900
And now even the Captain's disappeared.

75
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:19,740
When it rains, it pours.

76
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,500
You don't even have your Yo-Yo anymore.

77
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,540
What's there to be smug about?

78
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,940
It's like a soldier getting his weapon confiscated.

79
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:29,340
What an absolute disgrace.

80
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:31,740
How do you guys know about that?

81
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:36,030
Who are we? We've got eyes like hawks!

82
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,500
And ears like bats!

83
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:40,380
Oh, right!

84
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:43,260
I remember your Yo-Yo's called Nuclear Fission, right?

85
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,620
Sounds pretty scary.

86
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:49,500
Too bad it's just a paper tiger.

87
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,380
I think from now on, we should call it

88
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,300
"Nuclear Fool" instead!

89
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:03,420
What're you doing -Absurd!

90
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:11,580
That Jacky...

91
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,960
He doesn't seem fazed at all that Mark beat him.

92
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:16,830
He's just strutting around, all smug.

93
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,300
Something's definitely fishy here.

94
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,890
It's like they already know exactly

95
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,580
what that Masked Guy did.

96
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,940
Hey! Meatball!

97
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:31,260
When you faced off against that Masked Guy yesterday,

98
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,660
did anyone from Chengnan Team see it happen?

99
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:36,060
There wasn't a single soul around.

100
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,460
Then how could they know so much?

101
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:40,860
I've been wondering that too.

102
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:45,200
You think that Masked Guy might be some
hired Assassin from Chengnan Team?

103
00:08:46,210 --> 00:08:48,540
He's not an Assassin. He's more like a Hitman. A Pro.

104
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,460
A Pro at destroying our Yo-Yos.

105
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:51,900
Doesn't that make him an Assassin?

106
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,430
Do you think the Captain's Yo-Yo might...

107
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:56,700
Don't jinx it!

108
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,500
You go and try to get some information.

109
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:01,980
Me?

110
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Who else?

111
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:04,830
What about that Zoe?

112
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:06,300
Isn't she the perfect way to get to them?

113
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:07,260
Her?

114
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,660
I'm not going. You go if you want to.

115
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:14,460
What good would I be for that? Use your brain for once.

116
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:15,900
Fine, I'll go.

117
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:17,340
Don't make things worse.

118
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,220
Just do it for the Captain.

119
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,140
For the sake of Jianghai Team.

120
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:24,540
Just make a little sacrifice.

121
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,420
It's not like it's a huge sacrifice anyway.

122
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,780
Sacrifice your good looks.

123
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,700
Stop talking nonsense!

124
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,500
Alright, I'll go give it a shot.

125
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,220
Matthew...

126
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:47,580
Matthew!

127
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,420
Hey, Matthew! Why are you running?

128
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:54,750
I... I was just looking for you.

129
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:59,340
Looking for me? Then why run? You look so silly.

130
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,380
I... I wanted to talk to you about something.

131
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:06,780
Okay! Let's go talk by the river.

132
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,220
The view there is amazing.

133
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,560
No. No, let's not go to the river.

134
00:10:10,570 --> 00:10:12,060
It's rare for you to visit.

135
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,550
I've gotta take you to see my favorite spot!

136
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:16,860
Let's just talk right here.

137
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:18,780
Fine. Say what you've gotta say.

138
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,700
I just wanted to ask if you know anything

139
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:23,580
about this Mysterious Masked Guy.

140
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,500
and what his connection is to your Chengnan Team.

141
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,380
You came all this way just to ask me that?

142
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,300
Yeah. Why else would I be looking for you?

143
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:34,140
What? You're the worst! Don't ever come find me again!

144
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,740
So?

145
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:00,060
You thought you were so cool,

146
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,580
trying to use a honey trap like in the movies!

147
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:07,750
T-Teddy was the one who told me to find her!

148
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:11,840
This is bad. Really bad.

149
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:13,980
Mark lost his Yo-Yo, too.

150
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:15,900
How do you know that?

151
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,260
I left early this morning, and ran right into Mark.

152
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,140
He... he... get me some water, quick!

153
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:27,910
Don't panic. Just take it slow.

154
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:31,740
That Masked Guy...

155
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:35,100
That Masked Guy is seriously incredible!

156
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:40,860
A once-in-a-lifetime Master has finally appeared!

157
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:58,740
So you're the one with the mask, huh?

158
00:11:59,080 --> 00:11:59,910
And you must be Mark.

159
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:01,020
Glad you know.

160
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,420
Give me back Chuck's Nuclear Fission! Now!

161
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:05,340
You think it'll be that easy?

162
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:10,140
I'm actually very interested in your Speed Dragon.

163
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,060
You seem to know a lot about us.

164
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:14,940
If I beat you,

165
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:16,860
you have to give us back the Yo-Yos.

166
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,310
I won't go back on my word.

167
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,140
Get ready!

168
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,260
So where's the Captain now?

169
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:20,700
No idea.

170
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,590
As soon as I saw the Captain lose,

171
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,060
I ran straight back here to tell everyone.

172
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:26,940
How could you just leave the Captain there all by himself?

173
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,380
That's totally messed up!

174
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:30,300
Enough arguing, everyone.

175
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,740
Let's hurry up and find him!

176
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:40,860
Captain! Captain!

177
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,300
Look! The Captain's up ahead!

178
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,670
Hurry up!

179
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:45,660
Captain!

180
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:48,060
Come on, let's go!

181
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:50,460
Captain!

182
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:51,870
We were so worried about you!

183
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:53,820
What happened?

184
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,700
Mark, what on Earth happened?

185
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,100
Captain!

186
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,420
The Masked Guy said if we want the Yo-Yos back,

187
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:04,860
someone has to beat him.

188
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,190
He'll be waiting in the forest every day.

189
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,180
Only one person can go at a time.

190
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:12,060
If anyone follows, he won't show up.

191
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,460
And also, if a single day passes

192
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,140
with no one coming to challenge him,

193
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:19,740
the Yo-Yos he took from us will disappear forever.

194
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:21,660
What? What do we do now?

195
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,580
How did he pull off that Move?

196
00:14:24,330 --> 00:14:25,500
Yeah.

197
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:27,900
His throw is incredibly fast.

198
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:29,340
I couldn't even track his hand movements.

199
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:32,220
All I saw were countless shadows flying right at me.

200
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:33,660
And then my Yo-Yo was just... gone.

201
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,940
That's the exact same Move he used on me that day!

202
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,940
He snatched my Yo-Yo away just like that.

203
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,820
So it's a variation of Twin Dragons Rising.

204
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:42,980
Thousand Dragons Rising!

205
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,060
That Masked Guy is pure evil.

206
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,500
He only allows one person per day.

207
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:51,420
And if no one goes,

208
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:53,110
then the Yo-Yos he's holding

209
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:54,300
will be gone forever.

210
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,140
Is he seriously trying to wipe out

211
00:14:58,400 --> 00:15:00,060
our entire Jianghai Team by taking our Yo-Yos.

212
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:00,990
Exactly.

213
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,940
Wouldn't that mean our whole
Team gets completely crushed?

214
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,380
Don't say that.

215
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:06,780
Looks like we'll have to send our Best Player tomorrow.

216
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,220
It's the only way to stop his plan.

217
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:09,180
Yeah, for sure.

218
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,540
Leo, you're the only one on the
Team who's ever beaten Mark.

219
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:14,940
And since Mark lost,

220
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,820
you're the only real Pro we've got left.

221
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,580
I'm exhausted. I'm going to bed.

222
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,220
What's that supposed to mean?

223
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,500
I always knew he was completely heartless.

224
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:40,380
But you guys just had to treat him like some Superstar.

225
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,300
I really misjudged him this time.

226
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:46,000
What good is a guy with skills but no character?

227
00:15:46,010 --> 00:15:47,100
He's nothing.

228
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:49,500
You're just blindly obsessed with him.

229
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:51,420
I never expected it either.

230
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:53,820
I didn't think Leo would be so disloyal.

231
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:56,220
I warned you before.

232
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,620
You just didn't get it. So clueless.

233
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:00,540
When did you ever warn me?

234
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:02,460
You want me to spell it out for you?

235
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:03,900
Of course I could only drop hints.

236
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:10,140
Honestly, I don't even know who among you should go.

237
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:13,020
But someone has to do it!

238
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:17,340
How about this?

239
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:19,740
I say we just draw straws to decide.

240
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:23,100
Alright, that's actually a good idea.

241
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:01,980
I drew the short straw.

242
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:05,820
Then tomorrow it's all on you.

243
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,180
My skills aren't anything special,

244
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:12,540
but I'll definitely give it my best shot.

245
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:17,340
Oh, and his Thousand Dragons Rising is seriously deadly.

246
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:18,780
Be careful.

247
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:22,620
I suggest using a variation of

248
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:24,540
the Nuclear Shockwave against him.

249
00:17:24,870 --> 00:17:26,460
Okay, no problem.

250
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,380
Good luck!

251
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:50,940
Can you just be quiet for a sec?

252
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:52,860
I'm always quiet.

253
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:54,300
I'm not even talking.

254
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,660
The noises you're making are worse than you talking.

255
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:00,060
What? Sounds like you're just annoyed.

256
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:03,420
Here we go again.

257
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:05,820
You've done more sighing this
morning than in a whole year.

258
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,260
Isn't it annoying?

259
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:10,140
Yeah, why are you always sighing?

260
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:12,060
You're gonna jinx Matthew by doing that!

261
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,700
Why isn't Matthew back yet anyway?

262
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:42,960
Leo!

263
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:48,540
H- How could you be like this?

264
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,010
How can you just stand by and do nothing?

265
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:01,020
It wouldn't make a difference even if I went.

266
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:02,940
I'd just lose too.

267
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:06,640
But sending Matthew gives us even less of a chance!

268
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:08,700
How can you just stand there

269
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,610
and watch everyone lose their Yo-Yos?

270
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:19,710
You coward!

271
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:48,060
We know you gave it everything you had.

272
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,390
Captain, that slippery jerk didn't

273
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:52,380
even use Thousand Dragons Rising.

274
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:54,300
He was only using one hand.

275
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:57,660
And that Nuclear Shockwave variation you told me to try,

276
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:00,060
it was totally useless.

277
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:02,460
Right as I was using Phantom Shockwave to catch my Yo-Yo,

278
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:05,340
his hand shot out like a bolt of lightning.

279
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:06,780
And just like that, he snatched my Yo-Yo.

280
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,210
Hand over the Jianghai Team's Yo-Yos! Now!

281
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:20,700
Oh, you came. But you're just here
to hand me another Yo-Yo, aren't you?

282
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,060
Let me show you what I've got!

283
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:53,820
Jacky! Get out here!

284
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:59,580
What're you doing here?
You are not allowed to be here.

285
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,820
Jacky, you know you can't beat us fair and square,

286
00:21:05,910 --> 00:21:06,820
so you're playing dirty tricks.

287
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,220
That's just pathetic!

288
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:11,810
Anyone know what he's going on about?

289
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,980
Sounds like he's pretty worked up.

290
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,910
Stop playing dumb! You're just trying to deny it!

291
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:19,740
I'm warning you, getting up in my face like this

292
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,660
is seriously rude.

293
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:23,580
You guys are acting like total scumbags!

